der a microscope of stereotype, carry the resilience of her ancestors to embrace their existence?Between mystical visits from an ancient ancestor, every-day life at her job at her Uncle's convenience store on the Rez, and her community rallying to tear down a statue of her city's founder, Brooke feels torn. She is struggling to reconcile her Mi'kmaw heritage and living in a place founded by a British military officer hell bent on destroying her ancestors.\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Personnel</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Lisa Nasson</strong> | Brooke<br /><strong>Yolanda Bonnell</strong> | Emily<br /><strong>Devin MacKinnon</strong> | Good Guy / Fisherman Fred<br /><strong>Trina Morgan</strong> | Tammy<br /><strong>Jeremy Proulx</strong> | Uncle Chris</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1449\" height=\"1449\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?w=1449&amp;ssl=1 1449w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=1024%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=768%2C768&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=1120%2C1120&amp;ssl=1 1120w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Lisa-Nasson.jpeg?resize=640%2C640&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1449px) 100vw, 1449px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Lisa Nasson</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Lisa Nasson is a Mi’kmaq Actor, Director and Teacher from Millbrook First Nation in Nova Scotia. Lisa attended Neptune Theatre’s Professional program, and George Brown Theatre School where she studied Acting and Performance Studies. Lisa has also been an arts educator for many years, in subjects of acting, comedy and musical theatre at the Neptune Theatre School, and Young People’s Theatre. She has been working as an actor since leaving George Brown College, and is excited to jump into a new area of the theatre business. Some of her recent theatre credits include, <em>Offensive Fouls</em> (Neptune Theatre), <em>Vivaldi’s Ring of Mystery</em> (Neptune Theatre), <em>Spirit Horse</em> (Roseneath Theatre), <em>Munschtime!</em> (Young Peoples Theatre), <em>Lullaby</em> (Eastern Front Theatre), and <em>Fatty Legs</em> (Xara Choral Theatre).</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2025/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2025\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
