    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1024\" height=\"503\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Mozongi-photo-credit-Pierre-Manning-Audré-Desnoyers-Shootstudio-1024x503.jpg\" alt=\"Nyata Nyata\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Mozongi-photo-credit-Pierre-Manning-Audré-Desnoyers-Shootstudio-1024x503.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Mozongi-photo-credit-Pierre-Manning-Audré-Desnoyers-Shootstudio-300x148.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Mozongi-photo-credit-Pierre-Manning-Audré-Desnoyers-Shootstudio-768x378.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Mozongi-photo-credit-Pierre-Manning-Audré-Desnoyers-Shootstudio-1120x551.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Mozongi-photo-credit-Pierre-Manning-Audré-Desnoyers-Shootstudio-640x315.jpg 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\">\n<img width=\"1024\" height=\"681\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/DSC01933-1024x681.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/DSC01933-1024x681.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/DSC01933-300x200.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/DSC01933-768x511.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/DSC01933-1536x1022.jpg 1536w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/DSC01933-1120x745.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/DSC01933-640x426.jpg 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/DSC01933.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\">\n<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Nyata-Nyata-153132964772900/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\nFacebook-f\n</a>\n<a href=\"https://vimeo.com/97153831\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\nVimeo\n</a>\n<h2>Compagnie     Danse     Nyata     Nyata&nbsp;Mozongi</h2>\n<strong>Type of Performance:</strong> Dance\n\n<strong>Dates: </strong>September 15th @ 7pm <em>(Artist Talkback)</em>\n\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; September 16th @ 8pm\n\n<strong>Venue: </strong>Gladstone Theatre\n\n<strong>Run Time: </strong>55 minutes\n\n<strong>Ticket Prices: </strong><strong>$23</strong> <em>(Gen Ticket) </em>/ <strong>$19</strong><em> (Sr./Student)</em>\n\nFounded by Artistic Director Zab Maboungou, Montreal’s Compagnie Danse Nyata Nyata is a living laboratory where research, theory, and training provide for a unique approach to movement, rhythm and gesture.\n\nNyata Nyata is a contemporary dance company that teaches dance that supports dance technique trains dancers, produces staged and off-stage work, develop audiences, and actively participates in the institutional renewal of art policies. After 30 years of tireless work in creation and teaching, the company has earned an enviable reputation both in Canada and abroad.\n\nZab Maboungou’s choreography takes shape at the heart of the musical architecture of bodies and space where movement of the dancers’ bodies, the musicians, the instruments, and time are woven together and presented within an integrated scenography of sounds and gestures.\n\nCompagnie Dance Nyata Nyata is performing Mozongi at Prismatic 2019. It is a piece about time, and more precisely, about the physics of time. The step is weight and weight is time. Not repetition, but persistence.\n\nThe structure of Mozongi unfolds through the contrasts of movement and of immobility, of the one and of the many, in order to give shape to a primordial conflict – that of time which consumes space.\n\nPrismatic is delighted to have Mozongi perform at the Gladstone Theatre in Ottawa. &nbsp;\n\n<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2019-archive/\" role=\"button\">\nBack to 2019\n</a>"
