      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1024\" height=\"769\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Ensemble-Kamaan-1024x769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Ensemble-Kamaan-1024x769.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Ensemble-Kamaan-300x225.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Ensemble-Kamaan-768x577.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Ensemble-Kamaan-1120x841.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Ensemble-Kamaan-640x481.jpg 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\">\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"right\"><b>Amir Amiri | </b>Santur, Composer, Cultural Inventor<b></b></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"right\"><b>Behnza Sohrabi | </b>Tar (long-neck Persian lute) Rabab &amp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"right\">Daf (Iranian percussion instrument)</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"right\"><b>Showan Tavakol | </b>Kamancheh, Composer</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"right\"><b>Olivier Marin | </b>Viola, Soloist &amp; Chamber Musician,&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"right\">Composer</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ensemblekamaan/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\nFacebook-f\n</a>\n<a href=\"https://twitter.com/ensemble_kamaan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\nTwitter\n</a>\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yXdhmvrphvs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\nYoutube\n</a>\n<h2>Ensemble Kamaan</h2>\n<strong>Type of Performance:</strong> &nbsp;Concert\n\n<em>(shared bill performance with <a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/digging-roots/\">Digging Roots</a>)</em>\n\n<strong>Dates: </strong>September 17th @ 9pm\n\n<strong>Venue: </strong>Arts Court Theatre - Studio\n\n<strong>Ticket Prices: </strong><strong>$18</strong> <em>(Gen Ticket) </em>/ $<strong>16</strong><em> (Sr./Student)&nbsp;</em>\n\nEnsemble Kamaan offers a world of epic journeys - free from borders - with pieces that broaden the fields of musical traditions. Four musicians create a unique fusion that combines the refinement of traditional Persian classical music with the rigor of folk melodies in a contemporary and creative approach.&nbsp;\n\nIn the eclectic musical universe of the Kamaan Ensemble, boundaries are abolished and give way to a bewitching alchemy between the santour of Amir Amiri, the kamanche of Showan Tavakol, Behnaz Sohrabi’s rabab and voice, and Olivier Marin's viola.&nbsp; The energy of the Ensemble members blend together to evoke ancient and nostalgic tales with universal resonances.&nbsp;\n\nInspiration and sounds are pulled from Persian, Azerbaijan, Kurdish, Baluchi, Khorasani and Turkaman influence. Kamaan's objective is to link the written repertoire of Dastgahi music with the oral repertoire of the different regions in a contemporary musical perspective while exploring bridges with Western, Baroque and Medieval music.&nbsp;\n\nSet off on a road of tales and legends from Persia to Canada. Come to Prismatic 2019 to witness a musical discovery at the crossroads of civilizations - it is not to be missed\n\n<img width=\"1024\" height=\"989\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/2017-02-10-Kamaan_005-1024x989.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/2017-02-10-Kamaan_005-1024x989.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/2017-02-10-Kamaan_005-300x290.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/2017-02-10-Kamaan_005-768x741.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/2017-02-10-Kamaan_005-1120x1081.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/2017-02-10-Kamaan_005-640x618.jpg 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\">\n<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2019-archive/\" role=\"button\">\nBack to 2019\n</a>"
      }
    ],
