urses surrounding the Iranian diaspora. She aims to contribute to the interdisciplinary field of contemporary art within a Canadian cultural framework and help fill the gap of research and art production surrounding the Iranian-Canadian diaspora in cultural production and scholarship.</p><p><strong>SuperNova </strong></p><p>Presented in partnership with the Art Gallery of Nova Scotia, SuperNova takes audiences to galaxy Messier 82 to witness a talent show that sets an ideal stage to critically examine race and ethnic performance.</p><p>The judges in the talent show, Sirius, Mira and Bellatrix, are each named after the brightest star from various constellations. They are assessing the contestants, Oreo, Fatimeh, and Coco, who each perform short acts that examine issues of race and ethnic performance. As the show progresses, it becomes apparent that each judge is, themselves, mirrored by the Contestants.</p><p>Prismatic and the Art Gallery of Nova Scotia are honoured to debut Rah-Eleh’s SuperNova.</p><p>Join us for an artist talk with Rah-Eleh to dive deeper into the themes and concepts of this new work on Thursday September 13th at 6:00 pm at the Windsor Foundation Lecture Theatre at the AGNS.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2018-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2018\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
