    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"983\" height=\"656\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/ZAYO2.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/ZAYO2.jpg 983w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/ZAYO2-300x200.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/ZAYO2-768x513.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/ZAYO2-640x427.jpg 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 983px) 100vw, 983px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong> Esie Mensah -</strong> Choreographer &amp; Dancer  </p><p><strong>Samson Brown</strong> - Production Stage Manager</p><p><strong>Daniele Guevara</strong> - Lighting &amp; Projection designer</p><p><strong>Alexandra Lord</strong>- Costume Designer</p><p><strong>Esie Mensah, Percy Anane-Dwumfour, Miranda Liverpool, </strong></p><p><strong>Benjamin Williams, Marie Anne Ross, Amanda </strong><strong>Videla – </strong>Dancers</p>  \t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC48XddbqoNo8SSU1sioBLGA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTwitter\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/esiemensah/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.esiemensah.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tDesktop\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC48XddbqoNo8SSU1sioBLGA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tYoutube\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Esie     Mensah     Creations&nbsp;Zayo</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Type of Performance:</strong> Dance</p><p><strong>Dates: </strong>September 17th @ 8:30pm</p><p>              September 18th @ 7pm</p><p><strong>Venue: </strong>Nouvelle Scene - Studio B</p><p><strong>Runtime: </strong>30 minutes</p><p><strong>Ticket Prices: </strong><strong>$23 </strong><em>(Gen Ticket) </em>/ <strong>$19</strong><em> (Sr./Student)</em></p>\t\t\n\t\t<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Esie Mensah is an award-winning and Dora nominated dancer, choreographer, and creative director who has worked with some of the industry’s biggest icons such as Rihanna, Drake, French Montana, Janelle Monae, Nelly Furtado and more. </p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Esie  is committed to bringing a fresh new genre of dance into the industry. Afrofusion is her own unique style of dance that includes movements from traditional and contemporary African, Contemporary and Urban styles. </p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Beyond choreographing for dance performances, Esie has also worked with internationally recognized theatre companies as a movement director for Soulpepper Theatre, Shaw Festival, and Obsidian Theatre.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Her original creation, Zayo, has received top reviews from NOW Magazine and My Entertainment World and will be performed at Prismatic 2019.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">ZAYO is a memoir of Esie Mensah and an ode to Africa with the exploration of Esie’s Afrofusion movement in a new, fresh and contemporary way.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">In ZAYO, Ouhna arrives in the world of Nxi and has one directive: get to their destiny. Through a series of tests that will measure her mental, physical, and emotional strength, she must do what it takes to complete her quest, or the journey will consume her. </p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">This piece uses movement and dance to showcase the obstacles and challenges  Esie has faced throughout her own artistic career. It is a piece that pays respect and gratitude towards her mentors who have helped guide her along her journey. In ZAYO, Esie Mensah creates an ethereal future world in this bold dance-theatre work about self-discovery, destiny, and personal strength.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPrevious\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNext\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2019-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2019\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
