      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h1>Plan Your Prismatic</h1>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"#setp17-tickets\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tReserve Your Tickets\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t<a href=\"#Accessibility\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tAccessibility\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t<a href=\"#safety\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tCOVID-19 Safety Procedures\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Prismatic-Arts-Festival-COVID-19-Waiver-2020-FINAL.pdf\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tCOVID-19 Waiver\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Prismatic-2020-Program.pdf\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"300\" height=\"300\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic-300x300.png\" alt=\"Prismatic-2020-program\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic-300x300.png 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic-150x150.png 150w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic-768x768.png 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic-1536x1536.png 1536w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic-1120x1120.png 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic-640x640.png 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Prismatic-2020-final-graphic.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Prismatic-2020-Program.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" role=\"button\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPrismatic 2020 Program\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n                September 17<p><h3>Join us for an evening of live music! </h3><p>Time: 7pm </p><p>Location: The Carleton </p></p>\n                Jah'Mila<p><p>Born with a melody in her heart and a fire in her soul, Jah’Mila is a beacon for Jamaican music and culture in Nova Scotia. Interlacing deep reggae with notes of jazz, R&amp;B, and soul, she brings music that is lyrically intelligent, masterfully delivered, tastefully arranged, and undeniably inspiring.</p><p><a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/jahmila-2020/\">Read More</a></p></p>\n                Owen O'Sound Lee<p><p>Owen O’Sound Lee is an artist, musician, songwriter, vocalist, and producer from Toronto, Ontario who is now based in Halifax, Nova Scotia. Come experience Soulful Vibes with O'Sound at the Carleton on Thursday evening!</p><p><a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/owen-osound-lee-2020/\">Read More </a></p></p>\n                September 19<p><table border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td id=\"m_-2401234180406410820text_div940\" align=\"left\" valign=\"top\" width=\"630\"><p><b><i>Shifting Verse</i></b><br />a Prismatic Arts Festival Production</p><p>Presented by<br />National Arts Centre English Theatre’s<br />Grand Acts of Theatre<br /><i>Marking this Moment</i></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>With performances by Jenelle Duval and Eastern Owl</p><p>Time: 7:30 pm </p><p>Location: Grand Parade</p></p>\n                Dinuk Wijeratne<p><p>Sri Lankan-born Dinuk Wijeratne is a JUNO, SOCAN, ECMA, and Masterworks award-winning composer, conductor, and pianist. </p><p><a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/jenelle-duval/\">Read More</a></p></p>\n                Clyde A. Wray <p><p>Clyde A. Wray was born in New York City but has made Saint John, New Brunswick his home for the past 14 years. He is an author of six books of poetry and has appeared in and initiated countless projects in poetry, music, theatre, dance, and spoken word over his lifetime. Join us at <em>Shifting Verse</em> on September 19<sup>th</sup> to hear some incredibly powerful poetry by Clyde A. Wray. </p><p><a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/clyde-a-wray-2020/\">Read More</a></p></p>\n                Liliona Quarmyne <p><p>Liliona Quarmyne is a choreographer, dancer, actor, singer, community organizer, and facilitator. Her work stems from the idea of the body as story, and is particularly focused on the relationship between art and social justice, the body’s ability to carry ancestral memory, and the role the performing arts can play in creating change. Liliona is the Director of Choreography for <em>Shifting Verse</em> and will be dancing at this incredibly special show on September 19<sup>th</sup> 2020!</p><p><a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/liliona-quarmyne-2020/\">Read More</a></p></p>\n                Eastern Owl<p><p>Eastern Owl is an Indigenous-led, all nations group of women who blend the styles of First Nations drum, music, and contemporary folk to create their own innovative sound.</p><p><a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/eastern-owl/\">Read More </a></p></p>\n                Jenelle Duval<p><p>Jenelle Duval is a singer and songwriter from St. George’s, Ktaqmkuk (the island of Newfoundland). Her work is centred in contemporary narrative spertaining to her relationship with the land, Mi’kmaq identity, language, and reclamation of cultural practices.</p><p><a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/jenelle-duval/\">Read More</a></p></p>\n\t\t<p>Tickets</p><h3> <strong>Jah'Mila &amp; Owen O'Sound Lee</strong></h3><h3>September 17 @ 7pm at The Carleton | Sold Out!</h3><p>To add yourself to the waitlist email info@prismaticfestival.com</p><h4>General Admission : $20+tax<br />Student/Senior/Underwaged : $10+tax</h4><p><strong>Due to the COVID-19 pandemic, our ticketing system is a bit different from previous years. Thank you for your patience!</strong></p><p>1) Please send an email to info@prismaticfestival.com with the following information:</p><p><strong>First and last name:</strong></p><p><strong>Email:</strong></p><p><strong>Phone:</strong></p><p><strong>Number of people in party:</strong></p><p><strong>Number of General Admission tickets ($20+tax):</strong></p><p><strong>Number of Student/Senior/Underwaged tickets ($10+tax):</strong></p><p><strong>Has anyone in your party been outside of the Atlantic bubble</strong></p><p><strong> within the last 14 days?:</strong></p><p><strong> </strong><strong>Is anyone in your party under 19 years of age? </strong></p><p><strong>(If so, we will provide guidelines for their attendance.):</strong></p><p>2) The Prismatic team will be in touch with your request to confirm the reservation and conduct payment</p><p>3) Once you have paid through the link you are reserved!</p><p><strong>If you have any trouble with this method, or if it is inaccessible to you please call us at <a href=\"tel:902-425-6812\">902-425-6812</a> and we will personally assist you. Thanks!</strong></p>\t\t\n\t\t<h3><strong>Prismatic Arts Festival Safety Procedures and Guidelines at The Carleton</strong></h3><p>- Attendees will also be required to sign a COVID-19 waiver upon arrival and provide contact information, which will be used for contact tracing if necessary.</p><p>- all attendees are required to wear masks upon arrival, departure, or when using the bathroom</p><p>- attendees must remain at their table (table service will be provided during the show)</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Prismatic-2020-COVID-19-Health-and-Safety-Plan-The-Carleton-1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" role=\"button\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTo read our full procedure, click here!\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t<h1>Accessibility</h1>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Prismatic Arts Festival is committed to making all its programming fully accessible to all members of the community. This means we choose venues with accessible entrances, and personal support workers and service animals are always welcome at our events. </p><p><strong> </strong><strong>The Carleton</strong></p><p><strong> </strong>The entrance to The Carleton is on Argyle Street and requires the use of two steps, but a ramp is available for wheelchair access. If you would like to use the ramp, let us know at the time of booking or before the event so that we can ensure that it is set up by the time you arrive. Alternatively, you may call the phone number posted on the entrance door when you arrive to request a ramp or assistance.</p><p>Multiple single-user, gender-neutral, and wheelchair accessible washrooms are available at The Carleton.</p><p><strong> </strong>A Prismatic webpage with song lyrics will be available and can be accessed with a QR code at The Carleton. Wifi is available on site. To lessen our impact on the environment, limited print copies of song lyrics will be available – if you would like one, please let our Front of House staff know.</p><p><strong> </strong>Balloons will be available at all our music events for any Deaf or hard of hearing attendees who would like to use one to feel the vibrations of the music. Just ask our Front of House staff! </p><p><strong><em>Shifting Verse </em></strong><strong>at the Grand Parade</strong></p><p>Please be advised that <em>Shifting Verse</em> will include flashing lights, projections, loud audio, and a fog machine.</p><p><strong> </strong>Wheelchair accessible entrances to the Grand Parade are located on both Argyle Street and Barrington Street. These entrances are located on Argyle Street near Duke Street (next to City Hall) and on Barrington Street at George Street (across the street from TD Bank). Volunteers will be available at all entrances to assist you if needed. </p><p><strong> </strong>The Grand Parade is an outdoor venue and there are no washrooms on-site. There are public washrooms located 3 minutes away at Scotia Square (5201 Duke Street). The performance will be approximately 50 minutes long.</p><p><strong> </strong>The venue will be divided into social distancing boxes, and boxes near the stage area will be reserved for attendees with disabilities who require proximity to the stage. Please feel free to identify your needs to our volunteers – they can guide you to one of our reserved spaces. </p><p><strong> </strong>ASL interpretation will be available at <em>Shifting Verse</em>. The venue will be divided into social distancing boxes, and boxes near the interpreter will be reserved for attendees who require this service. </p><p><strong> </strong>A Prismatic webpage with the poetry text will be available and can be accessed with a QR code on-site.</p><p><strong> </strong>Balloons will be available at all our music events for any Deaf or hard of hearing attendees who would like to use one to feel the vibrations of the music. Just ask one of our volunteers!</p><p><strong> </strong>There are several benches, chairs, and picnic tables at the Grand Parade. We encourage you to arrive early or bring your own seating (eg., camping chairs) if you would like some. The show can be viewed from standing as well.</p><p><strong> </strong>Please feel free to approach our volunteers anytime for help or with any requests that would improve your access to the event. Our volunteers will be wearing Prismatic Volunteer pins, and there will be a volunteer and security guard stationed at each entrance.</p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Venues</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<h1>A Night of Live Music </h1>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"854\" height=\"536\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/The-Carleton-Argyle-Street-1.jpg\" alt=\"The-Carleton-Argyle-Street\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/The-Carleton-Argyle-Street-1.jpg 854w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/The-Carleton-Argyle-Street-1-300x188.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/The-Carleton-Argyle-Street-1-768x482.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/The-Carleton-Argyle-Street-1-640x402.jpg 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 854px) 100vw, 854px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><a href=\"https://www.thecarleton.ca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>The Carleton</strong></a></p><p>1685 Argyle St, Halifax, NS B3J 2B5</p><p>902-422-6335</p>\t\t\n<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d2838.555270202453!2d-63.57686068470464!3d44.64700579561737!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x4b5a23cd2786a4ab%3A0xd0a5dad6ecda57be!2sThe%20Carleton!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sca!4v1598723246337!5m2!1sen!2sca\" width=\"600\" height=\"450\" frameborder=\"0\" style=\"border:0;\" allowfullscreen=\"\" aria-hidden=\"false\" tabindex=\"0\"></iframe>\n\t\t\t<h1>Shifting Verse</h1>\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Grand Parade</strong></p><p>1770 Barrington St, Halifax</p><p> </p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1024\" height=\"30\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Thanks-sponsors-1024x30.jpg\" alt=\"Thanks to our Sponsors and Funders\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Thanks-sponsors-1024x30.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Thanks-sponsors-300x9.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Thanks-sponsors-768x22.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Thanks-sponsors-1120x33.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Thanks-sponsors-640x19.jpg 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"768\" height=\"386\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/funders-and-sponsors-2020-768x386.png\" alt=\"funders and sponsors-2020\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/funders-and-sponsors-2020-768x386.png 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/funders-and-sponsors-2020-300x151.png 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/funders-and-sponsors-2020-1024x515.png 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/funders-and-sponsors-2020-1536x773.png 1536w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/funders-and-sponsors-2020-1120x564.png 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/funders-and-sponsors-2020-640x322.png 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/funders-and-sponsors-2020.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" />"
      }
    ],
