    ],
    "http://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Onelight Theatre 2019"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"500\" height=\"333\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Asheq-2018-Exorcism-close-1120x745-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Asheq-2018-Exorcism-close-1120x745-1.jpg 500w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Asheq-2018-Exorcism-close-1120x745-1-300x200.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><b>Performance Credits </b></p><p><b>Director/Deviser</b> | Ed Roy <br /><b>Performer</b> | Shahin Sayadi<br /><b>Scenography </b>| Shahin Sayadi, Ed Roy<br /><b>Dramaturgy</b> | Ed Roy, Karen Bassett<br /><b>Touring Producer</b> | Ryan Cunningham for Cunning Concepts &amp;Creations Development<br /><b>Production Producer</b> | Maggie Stewart<br /><b>Onelight Theatre’s Producer and Artistic </b>Associate |  Rah-Eleh<br /><b>Stage Manager</b> | Pesch Napoose<br /><b>Set Designer</b> | Shahin Sayadi<br /><b>Live Action Video Designer</b> | Garry Kirkham<br /><b>Lighting Designer</b> | Chris Malkowski<br /><b>Sound Designer</b> | Reza Moghaddas<br /><b>Prop Designer</b> | Kei Yano<br /><b>Qlab, Mapping and Digital Technology </b>| Arian Yaghobei<br /><b>Original Video Design</b> | Shahin Sayadi, Nick Bottomley, Ryan Neal<br /><b>Original Music</b> | Habib Meftahboushehri, Mohsen Sharifian<br /><b>Theme Song and Additional Music</b> | Sina Bathaie<br /><b>Program Photo Credit</b> | Dahlia Katz</p><p><b><i>*Onelight would like to thank the Centre for Indigenous Theatre for their support and assistance.*</i></b></p><p><b>Development Credits </b></p><p><strong>Shahin Sayadi</strong> | Performer, Writer, Director, Scenographer, Set Design, Lighting and Projection Design, Sound Design, Set Construction, Costumes, Props, Music Arrangements, Videography, Photography, Film Production, Producer)<br /><strong>Maggie Stewart</strong> | Producer, Dramaturg<br /><strong>Raeesa Lalani</strong> | Stage Manager, Co-Producer, Sound Design, Tech Operator, Assistant Technical Director<br /><strong>Mohsen Sharifian</strong> | Composer, Musician, Cultural Advisor, selected music from Lian Music<br /><strong>Habib Meftahboushehri</strong> | Composer, Musician, selected music from Shibaali Album)<br /><strong>Sina Bathaie</strong> | Additional music selections from Ray of Hope album <strong>Karen Bassett</strong> | Dramaturg<br /><strong>Mike Mader</strong> | Technical Director, Lighting and Projection Design, Construction, QLab Supervisor and 3D mapping, Sound Installation <strong>Jake Dambergs</strong> | Digital Technology Advisor, Sound, Props<br /><strong>Nick Bottomley</strong> | Projections and Animation<br /><strong>Ryan Neal</strong> | Projection, Animation<br /><strong>Payam Sayadi</strong> | Calligraphy<br /><strong>Miya Turnbul</strong>l | Props<br /><strong>Shaun Alexander</strong> | Photography and Graphic Design<br /><strong>Hugh Nielson</strong> | Strategic Advisor<br /><strong>Coleen Shirin MacPherso</strong>n | Toronto Producer</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/onelighttheatre\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook-f\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://twitter.com/onelighttheatre\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTwitter\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/onelighttheatre/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Onelight     Theatre&nbsp;Asheq: Ritual Music to Cure a Lover </h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Type of Performance:</strong> Theatre</p><p><strong>Dates: </strong>September 16th @6pm</p><p>            September 17th @7pm</p><p>            September 18th @7:45pm</p><p>            September 19th @8pm</p><p><strong>Venue: </strong>Nouvelle Scene - Studio A</p><p><strong>Ticket Prices: </strong><strong>$23</strong> <em>(Gen Ticket) </em>/ <strong>$19</strong><em> (Sr./Student)</em></p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>For almost two decades, Onelight Theatre has been developing and producing thought-provoking, visually-stunning theatre works, that bring new voices, new perspectives and new ideas to the stage.</p><p>Founded and led by Artistic Director, Shahin Sayadi, Onelight Theatre emerged in the east coast in Halifax. In 2018, after providing the community with 16 years of excellence in theatre, Onelight  relocated and is now based in Toronto. We are excited to continue to develop and produce new works, tour our productions nationally and internationally, present the works of artists from across Canada and support the professional development of theatre artists through our Firestarter mentoring program.</p><p>Through the guided, disciplined working style established by Sayadi, Onelight develops new theatre works drawing from diverse cultural and artistic forms. Onelight is known not only for the compelling stories that it brings to the stage, but also for being at the forefront of innovative use of stage technology in scenography.</p><p> Onelight is currently the resident company of the Small World Music Centre in Toronto located in the Artscape’s Youngplace facility.  Onelight Theatre is working with Artistic Associate, Rah Eleh and theatre artist, Sarah Kitz, to develop new theatre works that will be debuted in 2020.</p><p>The pioneering Iranian-Canadian theatre artist Shahin Sayadi and director Ed Roy will be premiering a dynamic and newly conceived production of A<em>sheq: Ritual </em><em>Music to Cure a Lover </em>at Studio A of La Nouvelle Scene in Ottawa!</p><p><em>Asheq</em> is a reflection on contemporary life in Iran. While foregrounding the religious, social and political dimension that shape the experiences of Iranians today, Sayadi captivates audiences with his one-man performance and takes us on a journey to the shores of the Persian Gulf. This region is saturated with a rich<br />culture, eclectic music and dance that is rooted in East African and Persian traditions.</p><p>Sayadi seamlessly shifts between multiple characters and temporalities while weaving together inter-generational perspectives that provides a panoramic viewpoint into the struggles of a community transitioning from a traditional to modernsociety. Fighting darkness to step back into the light.</p><p>Sayadi reimagines mythological figures from classical Iranian poetry and fuses traditional icons and storytelling with theatrics and new technologies offering a delightful experience to the eyes and ears! Approaching the stage with a bold outlook and unforgettable performance, one unprecedented in Canadian theatre, <em>Asheq: Ritual Music to Cure a Lover,</em> is not to be missed!</p><p>Onelight will be presenting the world debut and a full run of <em>Asheq </em>in Toronto at the Small World Music Centre – Youngsplace Artscape, October and November 2019. <em>Asheq </em>is available for touring in 2020. Please contact Ryan Cunningham at Cunnning Concepts &amp; Creations to book the production.</p><p><strong><u>In the Press:</u></strong><em>“An enchantment of light and music” (NS Reviews, Halifax, Elissa Barnard)</em><em> </em><em>“Compelling and unique storytelling … staging that feels wholly immersive”</em><em> </em>(<em>The Way I See It Theatre Blog</em>)</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPrevious\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNext\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2019-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2019\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
