City of Vancouver artists residency.&nbsp;This is the first Artist Talk and Screening of Wong’s recent interdisciplinary and media art works in Ottawa in over a decade. It is not to be missed!\n\nThe illustrated talk will focus on art projects in public spaces including large scale architectural video mapping projections, commissioned neon for the Audain Art Museum, an outdoor video installation for Vancouver Opera and projects related to Occupying Chinatown in his year long residency commissioned by the City of Vancouver.\n<ul>\n \t<li>Year of Gif (2013) commissioned by Surrey Art Gallery</li>\n \t<li>No Thing is Forever (2016) commissioned &nbsp;by Audain Art Museum</li>\n \t<li>Five Octave Range (2017) commissioned by Vancouver Opera</li>\n \t<li>Winners &amp; Loser’s (2017) video mapping commissioned by Vancouver Art Gallery and Burrard Art Foundation</li>\n \t<li>Troublemaker’s 3.0 (2018)</li>\n \t<li>Occupying Chinatown (2019) commissioned by City of Vancouver Public Art Program</li>\n \t<li>Pride In Chinatown (2019) produced by On Main Gallery, Alternative Pride Festival</li>\n</ul>\n<img width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/4b_Five-Octave-Range-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/4b_Five-Octave-Range-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/4b_Five-Octave-Range-300x225.jpeg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/4b_Five-Octave-Range-768x576.jpeg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/4b_Five-Octave-Range-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/4b_Five-Octave-Range-1120x840.jpeg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/4b_Five-Octave-Range-640x480.jpeg 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/4b_Five-Octave-Range.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\