        "@value": "<img width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Santee-Smith-Prismatic-2017-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Santee Smith Prismatic Arts Festival 2017\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Santee-Smith-Prismatic-2017-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Santee-Smith-Prismatic-2017-300x300.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Santee-Smith-Prismatic-2017-150x150.jpg 150w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Santee-Smith-Prismatic-2017-768x768.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Santee-Smith-Prismatic-2017-640x640.jpg 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Santee-Smith-Prismatic-2017.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Artistic Direction/Choreography/Concept/Writer:</strong> Santee Smith<br /><strong>Performers:</strong> Santee Smith, Monique Mojica, Marina Acevedo<br /><strong>Video Performers:</strong> Nancy Wijohn, Bianca Hyslop<br /><strong>Music Co-producer/Score Arrangement:</strong> Cris Derksen<br /><strong>General Management:</strong> Cynthia Lickers-Sage<br /><strong>Production:</strong> Kaha:wi Dance Theatre</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.kahawidance.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tDesktop\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>by     Kaha:wi     Dance     Theatre&nbsp;Re-Quickening</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Type of Art:  Dance</p><p>Dates: Sept 21st, 22nd, 23rd @ 7pm</p><p>Location: Dal Arts Centre - Dunn Theatre</p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Her name is Tekaronhiáhkhwa Santee Smith and she is an Onkwehon:we woman from the Mohawk Nation Turtle Clan from Six Nations of the Grand River.</p><p>As beautiful as it is arresting, Santee Smith’s ground breaking piece Re-Quickening explores the intersection of Indigenous and new dance performance. Created through a process unique to her culture, Santee Smith’s Re-Quickening is a spiritual resurgence – a piecing together of shards of knowledge that tip colonialism on its head. Provoking, conceptual and visceral, this work is a timely call for re awakening. Kaha:wi Dance Theatre is one of Canada’s leading contemporary dance companies renowned for its artistry, creative excellence and collaboration, this is a chance to experience the best of the contemporary indigenous dance movement now taking the world by storm.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2017-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2017\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
