    ],
    "http://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A Tribe Called Red 2014"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1024\" height=\"682\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/KSF_8588-1024x682.jpg\" alt=\"A Tribe called Red Prismatic Arts Festival 2014\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/KSF_8588-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/KSF_8588-300x200.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/KSF_8588-768x511.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/KSF_8588-1536x1022.jpg 1536w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/KSF_8588-1120x746.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/KSF_8588-640x426.jpg 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/KSF_8588.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/atribecalledred\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://twitter.com/atribecalledred\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTwitter\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCQYo7hQsKKkHi4f0X-gB1yg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tYoutube\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://thehallucination.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tDesktop\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/atribecalledred/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>A     Tribe     Called     Red&nbsp;</h3>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Type of Art:</strong>  Music</p><p><strong>Dates: </strong>August 24th</p><p><strong>Location: </strong>Alderney Landing - Outdoor Mainstage</p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Bursting forth from Canada’s capital, native Producer/DJ crew <strong>A </strong>Tribe Called Red is producing a truly unique sound that’s impacting the global electronic scene and urban club culture.</p><p>Since 2010 the group—currently made up of DJ NDN, Bear Witness, and 2oolman—has been mixing traditional pow wow vocals and drumming with cutting-edge electronic music. Their self-titled album, released in March 2012, was long-listed for Canada’s prestigious Polaris Music Prize and included in the Washington Post’s top 10 albums of the year.</p><p>In a sense, ATCR’s music is the soundtrack to a contemporary evolution of the pow wow. Their Electric Pow Wow events in Ottawa showcase native talent and aboriginal culture, alongside an open wild party. Within a couple of years they’ve become the face of an urban Native youth renaissance, championing their heritage and speaking out on Aboriginal issues, while being on top of popular music, fashion, and art. Bear Witness doubles as the crew’s visual artist and creates stunning, political and sometimes humorous videos that incorporate film and pop culture references to native people and reclaim the aboriginal image. On May 7th, A Tribe Called Red released their second full-length album, Nation II Nation in Canada and in the USA on Tribal Spirit Music. The album was nominated on the shortlist of the Polaris Music Prize as one of the 10 best Canadian albums of the year and 4 APCMAs (Aboriginal Peoples Choice Music Award) for best group, best producer, best album and best cover art. ATCR have also collaborated and produced one of the last known Das Racist songs called Indians From All Directions as well as the song A Tribe Called Red on Angel Haze’s album Dirty Gold.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPrevious\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNext\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2014-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2014\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
