      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1024\" height=\"682\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/eh440-4-1024x682.jpg\" alt=\"eh440\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/eh440-4-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/eh440-4-300x200.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/eh440-4-768x511.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/eh440-4-1536x1022.jpg 1536w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/eh440-4-1120x746.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/eh440-4-640x426.jpg 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/eh440-4.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Eh440/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://twitter.com/eh440\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTwitter\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCMX4AkaiNEyaYNVjNlc0fww\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tYoutube\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>Eh440</h3>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Type of Art:</strong> Music</p><p><strong>Dates: </strong>Aug 22nd - 24th</p><p><strong>Location: </strong>Alderney Landing - Outdoor Mainstage</p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Eh440 started harmonizing together in 2012. Using just their voices, this Toronto-based acappella group has wow’d audiences across the USA and Canada. Now 2014 brings them to the next step in their journey—the release of their debut album Turn Me Up.</p><p>Eh440 is a mix of five people from five very different backgrounds and musical genres. Joe’s been a low bass singer his entire life, Luke’s an urban beatboxer, Janet identifies as a country/pop singer, Stacey’s soul/pop, and if that isn’t confusing enough, Mike’s even more of a musical chameleon who cites blues, folk, and anything with a good groove, as his influences. Together they form an unforgettable combination of crazy-ass beatboxing, sassy rapping, killer harmonies, and fresh, urban, RnB-influenced compositions. And their debut album, Turn Me Up, exemplifies their abundant influences.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPrevious\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNext\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2014-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2014\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
