        "@value": "Reeny Smith 2016"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1024\" height=\"766\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ReenySmith1-1024x766.jpg\" alt=\"Reeny Smith Prismatic Arts Festival\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ReenySmith1-1024x766.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ReenySmith1-300x225.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ReenySmith1-768x575.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ReenySmith1-1536x1150.jpg 1536w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ReenySmith1-1120x838.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ReenySmith1-640x479.jpg 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/ReenySmith1.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/iamreeny/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://twitter.com/iamREENY\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTwitter\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCs_R9yI2JEH1G2L7ezRImsg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tYoutube\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reenysmith/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Reeny Smith</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Type of Art:</strong>&nbsp; Music</p>\n<p><strong>Dates:&nbsp;</strong>Sept 25th&nbsp; @ 7pm </p>\n<p><strong>Location: </strong>Pier 21 - Kenneth C. Rowe Hall </p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Reeny Smith is an award winning singer/songwriter, from the musical powerhouse Smith family of North Preston, Nova Scotia. Commonly referred to as the “Canadian Alicia Keys,” Reeny has a smooth tone and powerful voice that will make you get in touch with your emotions as she takes you on a journey that will soothe your soul.</p><p>Reeny started singing and playing the piano as a young child and her roots singing in church provided a solid foundation for a promising career. An award-winning performer and the winner of the 2015 Casino Nova Scotia Artist in Residence Competition, Reeny has been part of the Prismatic Arts Festival since 2008. Her impeccable vocals leave audiences wanting more and Prismatic is thrilled to have her back this year to bring her outstanding musical talents to a national audience.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2016-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2016\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
