r-effects that stretched out to the whole world. Barbara is a direct descendant of this disaster and has choreographed this dance piece that brings the past to the present. It will haunt you, charm you, and bring new understandings of Indigenous people.</p><p>The performance of the Quebec Bridge Disaster will be part of Session 4 of The TALK: A Reconciliation 109 Years in the Making. In this session, Barbara will be joined by historians and members of the engineering community to explore how the Quebec bridge collapse affected different communities over the past century. </p><p>Prismatic is thrilled to present Barbara’s work and to facilitate a conversation with the wider community about the wide-ranging impacts of the 1907 Quebec Bridge collapse.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Presentation-Document.003-1024x576.jpeg\" alt=\"Barbara Diabo\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Presentation-Document.003-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Presentation-Document.003-300x169.jpeg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Presentation-Document.003-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Presentation-Document.003-1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Presentation-Document.003-1120x630.jpeg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Presentation-Document.003-640x360.jpeg 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Presentation-Document.003.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2016-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2016\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
