side. She earned a Bachelor of Music in Cello Performance at UBC and shared the title of Principal Cellist with the UBC Symphony Orchestra. She was also Curator in Residence at the Vancouver East Cultural Centre.</p><p>Cris Derksen was nominated for the Instrumental Album of the year at the 2016 Juno Awards.</p><p>We are thrilled to bring genre-defying musician Cris Derksen’s amazing sound to the Prismatic stage.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"960\" height=\"640\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/CrisDerksen3.jpg\" alt=\"Cris Derksen Prismatic Arts Festival\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/CrisDerksen3.jpg 960w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/CrisDerksen3-300x200.jpg 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/CrisDerksen3-768x512.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/CrisDerksen3-640x427.jpg 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2016-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2016\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
