      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"683\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/TamarDinaHeadshot-683x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Tamar Dina\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/TamarDinaHeadshot-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/TamarDinaHeadshot-200x300.jpg 200w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/TamarDinaHeadshot-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/TamarDinaHeadshot-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/TamarDinaHeadshot-1120x1680.jpg 1120w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/TamarDinaHeadshot-640x960.jpg 640w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/TamarDinaHeadshot.jpg 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 683px) 100vw, 683px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.musicliberatory.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tDesktop\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Tamar     Dina&nbsp;Music Liberatory </h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Type of Art:</strong>  Music</p><p><strong>Date: </strong>Sept 24th  @ 12pm</p><p><strong>Location: </strong>Halifax  Library - RBC Learning Centre </p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Music Liberatory is a Halifax-based non-profit, grassroots organization, founded by Tamar Dina, that works to dramatically increase the number of female instrumentalists by providing free music programs to women and girls with emphasis on developing and maintaining the cultural leadership of women of colour.</p><p><strong>Girls Got Song</strong> is a weekly singing group, founded by Music Liberatory, that promotes sisterhood and musical expression between girls aged 9-13. Girls have the opportunity to cover music written by female songwriters/musicians, as well as create and record original music created by the group.</p><p>Music Liberatory exemplifies Prismatic’s motto: Art for Everyone. We are pleased to share the work of Girls Got Song and Music Liberatory throughout Prismatic 2016. Also, Tamar Dina will be leading Session 6 of The TALK: Arts at the Grassroots, which will explore arts education as a tool of empowerment.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"896\" height=\"163\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/girlgotsong.png\" alt=\"Girls Got Song\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/girlgotsong.png 896w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/girlgotsong-300x55.png 300w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/girlgotsong-768x140.png 768w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/girlgotsong-640x116.png 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 896px) 100vw, 896px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2016-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2016\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
