      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"426\" height=\"640\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Shahin-Sayadi.jpg\" alt=\"Shahin Sayadi\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Shahin-Sayadi.jpg 426w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Shahin-Sayadi-200x300.jpg 200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 426px) 100vw, 426px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"mailto:shahin@prismaticfestival.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tEnvelope\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t<h2>Shahin Sayadi</h2>\t\t\n\t\t<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em><strong>Executive Director  </strong></em></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Shahin Sayadi is an established international artist who has made significant contributions to almost all aspects of performing arts in Canada and beyond. He was born and raised in Abadan, Iran and moved to Canada in 1986. Shahin studied technical scenography at Dalhousie University in Halifax, Canada.  Shahin has been an artistic and cultural leader in Canada for the past 20 years.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">In 2002, Shahin founded Onelight Theatre, where he is the Artistic Director. Through Onelight, Shahin writes, designs, directs and sometimes acts in original theatre works that have been performed across Canada and internationally. In 2008, Shahin founded the Prismatic Arts Festival, a professional multi-arts festival that showcases and celebrates the work of Canada’s leading Indigenous and culturally diverse artists.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"> In addition to his work with Onelight and Prismatic, Shahin is actively involved in national and regional advocacy and dialogue related equity, diversity and labour issues in Canadian arts. Shahin also regularly teaches workshops and masterclasses in scenography, theatre design, use of technology in theatre, and directing. </p>"
      }
    ],
