    "http://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Music 2014"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Music</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"423\" height=\"750\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/keonte-2.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/keonte-2.jpeg 423w, https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/keonte-2-169x300.jpeg 169w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 423px) 100vw, 423px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Keonté Beals</strong></p><p>Aug 23 &amp; 24</p><p>Alderney Landing Outdoor Mainstage</p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Keonté Beals sings R&amp;B, Soul and Gospel. His singing roots come from singing in Gospel choirs at his church Saint Thomas United Baptist Church. His style has often been compared to Luther Vandross, Anthony Hamilton, and John Legend. Singing smooth old-school R&amp;B but still keeping that Current R&amp;B vibe.</p><p>Keonté's voice has been said to consume incredible soulful vocal balance when singing ballads.</p><p>Be sure to check out Keont’e’s website and youtube channel, and stay tuned for his brand new album soon to be released!</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/z-smith3.jpg\" title=\"\" alt=\"\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2014-archive/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2014\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
