        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/son-latino-photo-1024x768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.sonlatino.ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tDesktop\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/sonlatinohfx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://twitter.com/sonlatinohfx?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTwitter\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.instagram.com/sonlatinohfx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t<p> </p><p><b>Mauricio Duarte</b><br /><b>Yonelis Legra Noa</b><br /><b>Jorge Loza</b><br /><b>Maykel Nuñez</b><br /><b>Paul St-Amand</b></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Son Latino</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Wednesday, September 29th | 7PM </p><p><strong><b>YouTube &amp; Facebook Live</b></strong></p><p><i>Free</i></p>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Featuring dynamic musicians from Cuba, Colombia, Mexico, and Canada, Son Latino puts a unique cross-cultural spin on Latin American music. The band is a favourite live ensemble for salsa dancers and Latin music aficionados in Halifax. </p><p>Son Latino’s repertoire is a mix of traditional and contemporary tunes from all over Latin America, and includes compulsively danceable rhythms like salsa, merengue, bachata, cha cha, and more. Son Latino’s instrumentation is reminiscent of a Cuban sexteto, featuring traditional percussion (congas, bongos, maracas, claves, guiro), bass, keyboard, trumpet, and vocals. Steeped in the tradition of Cuban son (the island’s pre-revolution folk and popular music) the band has performed several sold-out tributes to the great Buena Vista Social Club. </p><p>With driving rhythms, tight vocals, and improvisational flair, Son Latino makes it almost impossible for audiences to sit still.</p><p><i>Prismatic’s 2021 digital programming is generously supported by </i><b><i>TD Bank Group </i></b><i>and </i><b><i>Light House GO.</i></b></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/2021-2/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2021\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
