      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"621\" height=\"896\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DJELY-TAPA-web-1-3-e1658152138901.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DJELY-TAPA-web-1-3-e1658152138901.png?w=621&amp;ssl=1 621w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DJELY-TAPA-web-1-3-e1658152138901.png?resize=208%2C300&amp;ssl=1 208w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 621px) 100vw, 621px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<h2>English Bio:</h2>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Born into an illustrious lineage of griots, Djely Tapa is the daughter of the mythical griot and dancer Djely Bouya Diarra and of Kandia Kouyaté, one of Mali's greatest singers. Originally from the region of Kayes in western Mali, Djely Tapa has brought to the international stage the wise words and vocal art of the griots, emblematic figures of ancient and contemporary Malian society, whose origins date back to the Mandingo Empire of the 13th century. \"Masters of the word\" and depositaries of oral knowledge, musicians and kora players – the 21-stringed harp, their favorite instrument – the griots (djely, in Bambara language) are above all historians. In their metaphor-filled stories, they recount the genealogies of the Empire's nobles and the deeds of its warriors. </p><p>Based in Canada, Djely Tapa quickly integrated with the local scene. Among her experiences are important collaborations, such as Robert Lépine, Zal Cissoko, Afrotronix, the circus Kalabanté, Afrikana Soul Sister, and Abdoulaye Koné. Her encounters with experienced artists, for example with her compatriot Oumou Sangaré, the Mexican Claudia Martinez, or the Quebecer Sylvie Desgroseilliers, have suggested openings in terms of musical research and creation.</p><p>In February 2019, Djely launched <em>Barokan</em>, her first album. Reflecting her musical identity, this album is a resounding tribute to women and Africanness. With her high-pitched voice, incandescent delivery, and elegant gestures, Djely Tapa is a spectacular vocalist. Her dizzying flights of fancy fade into hushed whispers and leave the audience breathless, with a repertoire suspended between Sahelian atmospheres, blues, and electro. In May 2019, Djely was named Révélation Musique du Monde by Radio-Canada and in June 2020, her first album <em>Barokan</em> was named Best World Music Album at the 2020 Junos.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Djely     Tapa&nbsp;</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Sunday, October 9th | 7:30PM<br /><a style=\"color: #f3cf86;\" href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/our-venues#bus-stop\">Bus Stop Theatre</a><br />Regular $30 / Students, Seniors, &amp; Underwaged $15 / PWYC </p><p>Supported by <a style=\"color: #fff;\" href=\"https://afhalifax.ca/#/\">L'Alliance Française Halifax</a></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismatic.boldtypetickets.com/events/127680467/djely-tapa\" target=\"_blank\" role=\"button\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBuy Tickets  \n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t<h2>Version française:</h2>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Issue d’une lignée illustre de griots, Djely Tapa est la fille du mythique griot et danseur Djely Bouya Diarra et de Kandia Kouyaté, l’une des plus grandes cantatrices du Mali. Originaire de la région de Kayes, dans l’Ouest du Mali, Djely Tapa colporte sur la scène internationale le verbe empreint de sagesse et l’art vocal des griots, figures emblématiques de la société malienne ancienne et contemporaine, dont les origines remontent à l’Empire Mandingue du 13ème siècle. « Maîtres de la parole » et dépositaires de la connaissance orale, musiciens et joueurs de kora –la harpe à 21 cordes, leur instrument de prédilection-, les griots (djely, en langue bambara) sont avant tout des historiens. Dans leurs récits chargés de métaphores, ils déclinent les généalogies des nobles de l’Empire et les hauts faits de ses guerriers.</p><p>Installée au Canada, Djely Tapa a rapidement intégré la scène locale. Parmi ses expériences, des collaborations importantes, tel Robert Lépine, Zal Cissoko, Afrotronix, le cirque Kalabanté Afrikana Soul Sister et Abdoulaye Koné. Ses rencontres avec des artistes chevronnées, par exemple avec sa compatriote Oumou Sangaré, la mexicaine Claudia Martinez ou encore la québécoise Sylvie Desgroseillers, lui ont suggéré des ouvertures sur le plan de la recherche et de la création musicales.</p><p>En février 2019, Djely Tapa a lancé <em>Barokan</em>, son premier album. Reflet de son identité musicale, cet album est un hommage retentissant à la femme et à l’africanite. La voix haut-perchée, le débit incandescent, le geste élégant, Djely Tapa est une vocaliste racée. Ses envolées vertigineuses s’éteignent dans des murmures étouffés et laissent le public à bouche bée, avec un répertoire en suspens entre ambiances sahéliennes, blues et électro. En mai 2019, Djely Tapa a été nommée Révélation Musique du Monde de Radio-Canada et en juin 2020, son premier album <em>Barokan</em> a été nommée “Meilleur album musique du monde” aux Junos 2020.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/djelytapa/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg><use xlink:href=\"#fab-facebook\" /></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/djelytapa/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg><use xlink:href=\"#fab-instagram\" /></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1ZWqXYKC5ZOETTsGYVihTF?autoplay=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tSpotify\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg><use xlink:href=\"#fab-spotify\" /></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCZOsJXvqPg2PFhdwBjzWP3A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tYoutube\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg><use xlink:href=\"#fab-youtube\" /></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1007\" height=\"664\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DJELY-TAPA-web-2-e1656435944669.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DJELY-TAPA-web-2-e1656435944669.jpg?w=1007&amp;ssl=1 1007w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DJELY-TAPA-web-2-e1656435944669.jpg?resize=300%2C198&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DJELY-TAPA-web-2-e1656435944669.jpg?resize=768%2C506&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DJELY-TAPA-web-2-e1656435944669.jpg?resize=640%2C422&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1007px) 100vw, 1007px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<em>Photo credits: JYPHEAL / ETALLON Group (all) </em>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2022/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2022\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
