    "http://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "2022 SAMQWAN"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h1>SAMQWAN<br><p style=\"color: #F4C86F; font-size: 0.6em\">Sarah Prosper</p></h1>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"300\" height=\"233\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Pop-Up-Prismatic-logo-transparent-e1658861413543-300x233.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Pop-Up-Prismatic-logo-transparent-e1658861413543.png?resize=300%2C233&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Pop-Up-Prismatic-logo-transparent-e1658861413543.png?resize=1024%2C794&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Pop-Up-Prismatic-logo-transparent-e1658861413543.png?resize=768%2C595&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Pop-Up-Prismatic-logo-transparent-e1658861413543.png?resize=640%2C496&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Pop-Up-Prismatic-logo-transparent-e1658861413543.png?w=1080&amp;ssl=1 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Sunday,&nbsp;August&nbsp;14th - Monday, August 15th<br>Online&nbsp;<br>Free</p>\t\t\n\t\thttps://youtu.be/UC1gTMbmY9w<p>“Samqwan” is the Mi'kmaq word for water and this new multi-disciplinary show, will inspire and welcome you to experience the value of water from an Indigenous perspective, showing its sacredness, its purposes, and the gift of walking in two worlds – but also the responsibilities.</p><p>Ke'aknutama'tinej - Can we talk<br />Ke'amakaltinej - Can we dance</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Personnel</h2>\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Sarah Prosper</strong> | Creator &amp; Choreographer<br /><strong>Corey Katz</strong> | Production Photography<br /><strong>Lana Joy Gould Photography</strong> | Water Images</p><p><strong>Produced by Highland Arts Theatre </strong></p><p>Special thanks to Mi'kmaq community Elders: Albert Marshall, Doreen Bernard, &amp; Jane Meader<br />Singers / Composers: Eastern Owl, shalan joudry, Riley Mclean Dewitt, &amp; Msit No'kmaq (All My Relations) </p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1080\" height=\"1080\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Samqwan-personnel-list-.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Samqwan-personnel-list-.jpeg?w=1080&amp;ssl=1 1080w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Samqwan-personnel-list-.jpeg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Samqwan-personnel-list-.jpeg?resize=1024%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Samqwan-personnel-list-.jpeg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Samqwan-personnel-list-.jpeg?resize=768%2C768&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Samqwan-personnel-list-.jpeg?resize=640%2C640&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1080px) 100vw, 1080px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2022/\" role=\"button\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2022\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
