      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/about/#our-staff\">\n\t\t\t\t<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M257.5 445.1l-22.2 22.2c-9.4 9.4-24.6 9.4-33.9 0L7 273c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9L201.4 44.7c9.4-9.4 24.6-9.4 33.9 0l22.2 22.2c9.5 9.5 9.3 25-.4 34.3L136.6 216H424c13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24v32c0 13.3-10.7 24-24 24H136.6l120.5 114.8c9.8 9.3 10 24.8.4 34.3z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to Our Staff\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"512\" height=\"761\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/1-website-Sophie-Wilcott-Headshot-2023-Sophia-Wilcott.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/1-website-Sophie-Wilcott-Headshot-2023-Sophia-Wilcott.jpg?w=512&amp;ssl=1 512w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/1-website-Sophie-Wilcott-Headshot-2023-Sophia-Wilcott.jpg?resize=202%2C300&amp;ssl=1 202w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 512px) 100vw, 512px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Outreach Coordinator</h2>\t\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Sophie Wilcott</h2>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Sophie Wilcott (they/she) is a maritime-based, multidisciplinary theatre artist and performer.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Acting, directing, writing, dancing, administrating, and dramaturging, they have collaborated with Prismatic Arts Festival, Theatre Nova Scotia, Neptune Theatre, Prismatic Arts Festival, the Atlantic Repertory Company, Theatre New Brunswick, Playwrights Atlantic Resource Centre, The Unnatural Disaster Theatre Company, Voice Factory-La Boîte Vocale, Symphony New Brunswick, Connection Dance Works, and InterAction School of Performing Arts.</p><p>In spring of 2023, they received a Bachelor of Arts with Honours in Theatre (Acting) and a certificate in Dance &amp; Movement Composition from Dalhousie Fountain School of Performing Arts. Sophie is a recipient of the prestigious Dalhousie Chancellor’s Scholarship (2019-2023), the Fountain School of Performing Arts Undergraduate Scholarship (2019-2023), the Christine Zinck (Theatre) Scholarship (2022) and the Arts New Brunswick Scholarship in (2019 &amp; 2022). Their recent play-in-development, Maiden Names, won the PARC U-compete Audience Choice award (2023).</p>\n<p>Sophie prioritizes theatre that cultivates empathy and is rooted in the concept of human goodness. They view art as a means to show people and communities their potential. Sophie aims to bring theatre to the people &amp; invite audiences that are typically excluded from the world of theatre to participate in the consumption and creation of new works. They create work that asks audiences to laugh and celebrate the failures and successes of humanity.</p>"
      }
    ],
