hancellor’s Scholarship (2019-2023), the Fountain School of Performing Arts Undergraduate Scholarship (2019-2023), the Christine Zinck (Theatre) Scholarship (2022) and the Arts New Brunswick Scholarship in (2019 &amp; 2022). Their recent play-in-development, Maiden Names, won the PARC U-compete Audience Choice award (2023).</p>\n<p>Sophie prioritizes theatre that cultivates empathy and is rooted in the concept of human goodness. They view art as a means to show people and communities their potential. Sophie aims to bring theatre to the people &amp; invite audiences that are typically excluded from the world of theatre to participate in the consumption and creation of new works. They create work that asks audiences to laugh and celebrate the failures and successes of humanity.</p>"
