    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1032\" height=\"1521\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Anyma-IMG_8394-e1689868700321.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Anyma-IMG_8394-e1689868700321.jpeg?w=1032&amp;ssl=1 1032w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Anyma-IMG_8394-e1689868700321.jpeg?resize=204%2C300&amp;ssl=1 204w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Anyma-IMG_8394-e1689868700321.jpeg?resize=695%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 695w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Anyma-IMG_8394-e1689868700321.jpeg?resize=768%2C1132&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Anyma-IMG_8394-e1689868700321.jpeg?resize=640%2C943&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1032px) 100vw, 1032px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Anyma</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Saturday, September 30th | 2PM <br /><a style=\"color: #ded9e9;\" href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/our-venues#carleton\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Carleton</a></p><p>Co-presented with</p><p><img src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/HUFF_logo-removebg-preview.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"225\" height=\"225\" /></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.thecarleton.ca/events/prismatic-huff-anyma-leonard-sumner/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBuy Tickets\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t<p>Anyma is a Canadian electro-pop artist hailing from Wendake, Quebec. A member of the Wendat Nation, her music finds parallels in her Indigenous heritage and her roots as a professional composer and dancer.</p><p>Her debut EP, <em>Humans</em>, earned her multiple top ten positions at the Indigenous Music Countdown (peaking at #1), runner up in the 2021 SOCAN Indigenous Songwriter Awards, and thousands of spins via SiriusXM and CBC, among others. She has been a featured/cover artist with Canadian Musician, Toronto Star, and the Globe &amp; Mail. On YouTube, she averages hundreds of thousands of streams of her original performances, music videos, full-length animations, and more. While at DSPS, she has been featured on countless playlists – including a cover for Spotify’s Indigenous playlist as well as a feature on their On the Record program – equating to millions of streams worldwide across all platforms.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.anymamusic.com/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tGlobe\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 496 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M336.5 160C322 70.7 287.8 8 248 8s-74 62.7-88.5 152h177zM152 256c0 22.2 1.2 43.5 3.3 64h185.3c2.1-20.5 3.3-41.8 3.3-64s-1.2-43.5-3.3-64H155.3c-2.1 20.5-3.3 41.8-3.3 64zm324.7-96c-28.6-67.9-86.5-120.4-158-141.6 24.4 33.8 41.2 84.7 50 141.6h108zM177.2 18.4C105.8 39.6 47.8 92.1 19.3 160h108c8.7-56.9 25.5-107.8 49.9-141.6zM487.4 192H372.7c2.1 21 3.3 42.5 3.3 64s-1.2 43-3.3 64h114.6c5.5-20.5 8.6-41.8 8.6-64s-3.1-43.5-8.5-64zM120 256c0-21.5 1.2-43 3.3-64H8.6C3.2 212.5 0 233.8 0 256s3.2 43.5 8.6 64h114.6c-2-21-3.2-42.5-3.2-64zm39.5 96c14.5 89.3 48.7 152 88.5 152s74-62.7 88.5-152h-177zm159.3 141.6c71.4-21.2 129.4-73.7 158-141.6h-108c-8.8 56.9-25.6 107.8-50 141.6zM19.3 352c28.6 67.9 86.5 120.4 158 141.6-24.4-33.8-41.2-84.7-50-141.6h-108z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/musicanyma\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M504 256C504 119 393 8 256 8S8 119 8 256c0 123.78 90.69 226.38 209.25 245V327.69h-63V256h63v-54.64c0-62.15 37-96.48 93.67-96.48 27.14 0 55.52 4.84 55.52 4.84v61h-31.28c-30.8 0-40.41 19.12-40.41 38.73V256h68.78l-11 71.69h-57.78V501C413.31 482.38 504 379.78 504 256z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t