    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h2>Alan     Syliboy&nbsp;Wolverine and Little Thunder + Vistas: Little Thunder</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Wolverine and Little Thunder<br>Saturday, September 30th - Sunday, October 8th | 24 hour loop<br><a style=\"color: #ded9e9;\" href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/our-venues#rogers-square\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rogers Square</a></p>\n<p>Supported by</p><p><img src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/sponsor-logos-05.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\" /></p><p>Vistas: Little Thunder <br />Monday, October 2nd | 6:30PM<br /><a style=\"color: #ded9e9;\" href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/our-venues#citadel-hill\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Halifax Citadel Hill National Historic Site - North Front Casemates</a><br /><em>(registration required due to limited capacity)</em></p><p>Film provided courtesy of</p><p><img src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/ONF_Logo_blanc-white-300x181.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"181\" /></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismatic.tickethalifax.com/events/141706209/prismatic-after-dark\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFREE - Register Here\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"907\" height=\"798\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/2-website-Alan-Syliboy-fff-e1690222599910.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/2-website-Alan-Syliboy-fff-e1690222599910.jpg?w=907&amp;ssl=1 907w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/2-website-Alan-Syliboy-fff-e1690222599910.jpg?resize=300%2C264&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/2-website-Alan-Syliboy-fff-e1690222599910.jpg?resize=768%2C676&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/2-website-Alan-Syliboy-fff-e1690222599910.jpg?resize=640%2C563&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 907px) 100vw, 907px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Alan Syliboy grew up believing that native art was generic. “As a youth, I found painting difficult and painful, because I was unsure of my identity.” But his confidence grew in 1972 when he studied privately with Shirley Bear. He then attended the Nova Scotia College of Art and Design where, 25 years later, he was invited to sit on the Board of Governors. Syliboy looked to the Indigenous Mi’kmaq petroglyph tradition for inspiration and developed his own artistic vocabulary out of those forms. His popularization of these symbolic icons has conferred on them a mainstream legitimacy that restores community pride in Mi’kmaq heritage. </p><p>His 2010 Film, Little Thunder, an animated collaboration between Syliboy, director, Nance Ackerman, and animator, Paton Francis, has been screened at numerous film festivals, and received the Best Animation Film Award at the First Peoples Festival in Montreal.</p><p>Alan still lives and works in Millbrook, NS, where he was born and raised. He creates his art in his studio in Truro, NS.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://alansyliboy.ca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tGlobe\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 496 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M336.5 160C322 70.7 287.8 8 248 8s-74 62.7-88.5 152h177zM152 256c0 22.2 1.2 43.5 3.3 64h185.3c2.1-20.5 3.3-41.8 3.3-64s-1.2-43.5-3.3-64H155.3c-2.1 20.5-3.3 41.8-3.3 64zm324.7-96c-28.6-67.9-86.5-120.4-158-141.6 24.4 33.8 41.2 84.7 50 141.6h108zM177.2 18.4C105.8 39.6 47.8 92.1 19.3 160h108c8.7-56.9 25.5-107.8 49.9-141.6zM487.4 192H372.7c2.1 21 3.3 42.5 3.3 64s-1.2 43-3.3 64h114.6c5.5-20.5 8.6-41.8 8.6-64s-3.1-43.5-8.5-64zM120 256c0-21.5 1.2-43 3.3-64H8.6C3.2 212.5 0 233.8 0 256s3.2 43.5 8.6 64h114.6c-2-21-3.2-42.5-3.2-64zm39.5 96c14.5 89.3 48.7 152 88.5 152s74-62.7 88.5-152h-177zm159.3 141.6c71.4-21.2 129.4-73.7 158-141.6h-108c-8.8 56.9-25.6 107.8-50 141.6zM19.3 352c28.6 67.9 86.5 120.4 158 141.6-24.4-33.8-41.2-84.7-50-141.6h-108z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/alansyliboy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M504 256C504 119 393 8 256 8S8 119 8 256c0 123.78 90.69 226.38 209.25 245V327.69h-63V256h63v-54.64c0-62.15 37-96.48 93.67-96.48 27.14 0 55.52 4.84 55.52 4.84v61h-31.28c-30.8 0-40.41 19.12-40.41 38.73V256h68.78l-11 71.69h-57.78V501C413.31 482.38 504 379.78 504 256z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/syliboyalan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M224.1 141c-63.6 0-114.9 51.3-114.9 114.9s51.3 114.9 114.9 114.9S339 319.5 339 255.9 287.7 141 224.1 141zm0 189.6c-41.1 0-74.7-33.5-74.7-74.7s33.5-74.7 74.7-74.7 74.7 33.5 74.7 74.7-33.6 74.7-74.7 74.7zm146.4-194.3c0 14.9-12 26.8-26.8 26.8-14.9 0-26.8-12-26.8-26.8s12-26.8 26.8-26.8 26.8 12 26.8 26.8zm76.1 27.2c-1.7-35.9-9.9-67.7-36.2-93.9-26.2-26.2-58-34.4-93.9-36.2-37-2.1-147.9-2.1-184.9 0-35.8 1.7-67.6 9.9-93.9 36.1s-34.4 58-36.2 93.9c-2.1 37-2.1 147.9 0 184.9 1.7 35.9 9.9 67.7 36.2 93.9s58 34.4 93.9 36.2c37 2.1 147.9 2.1 184.9 0 35.9-1.7 67.7-9.9 93.9-36.2 26.2-26.2 34.4-58 36.2-93.9 2.1-37 2.1-147.8 0-184.8zM398.8 388c-7.8 19.6-22.9 34.7-42.6 42.6-29.5 11.7-99.5 9-132.1 9s-102.7 2.6-132.1-9c-19.6-7.8-34.7-22.9-42.6-42.6-11.7-29.5-9-99.5-9-132.1s-2.6-102.7 9-132.1c7.8-19.6 22.9-34.7 42.6-42.6 29.5-11.7 99.5-9 132.1-9s102.7-2.6 132.1 9c19.6 7.8 34.7 22.9 42.6 42.6 11.7 29.5 9 99.5 9 132.1s2.7 102.7-9 132.1z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://twitter.com/AlanSyliboy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTwitter\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M459.37 151.716c.325 4.548.325 9.097.325 13.645 0 138.72-105.583 298.558-298.558 298.558-59.452 0-114.68-17.219-161.137-47.106 8.447.974 16.568 1.299 25.34 1.299 49.055 0 94.213-16.568 130.274-44.832-46.132-.975-84.792-31.188-98.112-72.772 6.498.974 12.995 1.624 19.818 1.624 9.421 0 18.843-1.3 27.614-3.573-48.081-9.747-84.143-51.98-84.143-102.985v-1.299c13.969 7.797 30.214 12.67 47.431 13.319-28.264-18.843-46.781-51.005-46.781-87.391 0-19.492 5.197-37.36 14.294-52.954 51.655 63.675 129.3 105.258 216.365 109.807-1.624-7.797-2.599-15.918-2.599-24.04 0-57.828 46.782-104.934 104.934-104.934 30.213 0 57.502 12.67 76.67 33.137 23.715-4.548 46.456-13.32 66.599-25.34-7.798 24.366-24.366 44.833-46.132 57.827 21.117-2.273 41.584-8.122 60.426-16.243-14.292 20.791-32.161 39.308-52.628 54.253z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t<h2>Wolverine and Little Thunder</h2>\t\t\n\t\t<p>At once a universal story of friendship and problem-solving, Wolverine and Little Thunder is a contemporary invocation of traditional Mi’kmaw knowledge, reinforcing the importance of the relationship between the Mi’kmaq and eel, a dependable year-round food source traditionally offered to Glooscap, the Creator, for a successful hunt.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Personnel</h2>\t\t\n\t\t<p><b>Alan Syliboy </b>| Executive Producer, Animation Director &amp; Character Design<b><br />Luke Fancy </b>| Lead Animator<br /><b>Tim Allenby</b> | Animator<br /><b>Jeremy Kyle</b> | Animator<br /><b>Lukas Pearse</b> | Music &amp; Soundtrack Editor<br /><b>Alan Syliboy</b> | Musician<br /><b><br />Evan Syliboy</b> | Musician<br /><b>Hubert Francis</b> | Musician<br /><b>Aaron Prosper</b> | Musician<br /><b>Joanne Hatfield</b> | Musician<br /><b>Matt Gallant</b> | Musician<br /><b>Julianne Syliboy</b> | Musician<br /><b>Joel Plaskett </b>| Sound Engineer<br /><b>Thomas Stajcer</b> | Sound Engineer</p><p>Soundtrack Recorded at New Scotland Yard Studio </p><p>Produced with the assistance of the National Film Board of Canada – Filmmaker Assistance Program</p><p>Based on the book – “Wolverine and Little Thunder – An Eel Hunting Adventure by Alan Syliboy</p><p>In collaboration with animators from Cartoon Conrad and with Nimbus Publishing.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Vistas: Little Thunder</h2>\t\t\n\t\tThis animated short, inspired by the Mi'kmaq legend \"The Stone Canoe\" explores Indigenous humour. We follow Little Thunder as he reluctantly leaves his family and sets out on a cross-country canoe trip to become a man.\n\t\t\t<h2>Personnel</h2>\t\t\n\t\t<p><b>Nance Ackerman </b>| Writer, Director, Original Music, Sound Design <b><br />Alan Syliboy</b> | Writer, Director, Original Artwork<b><br />Paton Francis </b>| Assistant Director, Animation<br /><b>Jamie Alexander Alcorn</b> | Original Music, Sound Design<br /><b>Al Strickland </b>| Recording, Mixing<br /><b>Reynold Gregor</b> | Online Editing<br /><b>Candice Desormeaux </b>| Production Supervisor<br /><b>John William Lutz</b> | Administration<br /><b>Cyndi Forcand</b> | Administration<br /><b>Stephanie Coolen </b>| Production Coordinator<br /><b>Vanessa Larsen </b>| Production Coordinator<br /><b>Leslie Stafford </b>| Marketing Manager<br /><b>Amy Stewart Gallant</b> | Marketing Manager<br /><b>Vanessa Loewen</b> | Series Producer<br /><b>Joe MacDonald</b> | Series Producer<br /><b>Derek Mazur</b> | Series Executive Producer<br /><b>Peter Strutt</b> | Series Executive Producer<br /><b>Annette Clarke </b>| Producer<br /><b>Kent Martin</b> | Executive Producer</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2023/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2023\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
