      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 1000\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M646 125C629 125 613 133 604 142L308 442C296 454 292 471 292 487 292 504 296 521 308 533L604 854C617 867 629 875 646 875 663 875 679 871 692 858 704 846 713 829 713 812 713 796 708 779 692 767L438 487 692 225C700 217 708 204 708 187 708 171 704 154 692 142 675 129 663 125 646 125Z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 1000\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M696 533C708 521 713 504 713 487 713 471 708 454 696 446L400 146C388 133 375 125 354 125 338 125 325 129 313 142 300 154 292 171 292 187 292 204 296 221 308 233L563 492 304 771C292 783 288 800 288 817 288 833 296 850 308 863 321 871 338 875 354 875 371 875 388 867 400 854L696 533Z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Local     Artists     Community     Tour&nbsp;Moose & Hawk and Golden</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Wednesday, April 9th | 11:30AM<br />Wagmatcook Culture &amp; Heritage Centre<br />Followed by Artist Talkback</p><p>Co-presented with Neptune TourCo</p><p><img src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/TourCo-Banner-2.0-e1751481991363-300x135.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"159\" height=\"72\" /></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1080\" height=\"1080\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Moose-and-Hawk-poster.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Moose-and-Hawk-poster.jpg?w=1080&amp;ssl=1 1080w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Moose-and-Hawk-poster.jpg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Moose-and-Hawk-poster.jpg?resize=1024%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Moose-and-Hawk-poster.jpg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Moose-and-Hawk-poster.jpg?resize=768%2C768&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Moose-and-Hawk-poster.jpg?resize=640%2C640&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1080px) 100vw, 1080px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Moose     &     Hawk&nbsp;by Lisa Nasson </h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\tA youth activist is questioned by authorities after the statue of Edward Cornwallis loses his head. Brooke Stephens defends her actions while being interrogated in a police station. Inspired by true events, Brooke takes the audience and the hawk-like policewoman through the historical context of Mi’kmaq oppression. \t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Personnel:</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Lisa Nasson</strong> | Director / Playwright<br /><strong>Desna (Dez) Michael Thomas</strong> | “Brook”<br /><strong>Leah Pritchard</strong> | “Miss”<br /><strong>Sarah Mackenzie</strong> | Stage Manager</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1080\" height=\"1080\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Golden-poster.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Golden-poster.jpg?w=1080&amp;ssl=1 1080w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Golden-poster.jpg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Golden-poster.jpg?resize=1024%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Golden-poster.jpg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Golden-poster.jpg?resize=768%2C768&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Golden-poster.jpg?resize=640%2C640&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1080px) 100vw, 1080px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Golden&nbsp;by Daisy Rayne </h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\tMay is a biracial art student struggling to create a piece of art about her racial identity. With the help of a strange but friendly puppet, she explores her identity by visiting her childhood bedroom. In this room she reflects on her parent's rocky relationship (made worse by the prejudice against interracial marriages at the time) while trying to remember a piece of her past that could help finish the project. Golden is a story about discovery, racial identity, getting in touch with your childhood, and using art as a way to dig deeper.\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Personnel:</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Daisy Rayne</strong> | “May” / Playwright<br /><strong>Harmony Adesola</strong> | “William”<br /><strong>Leah Pritchard</strong> | “Julie”<br /><strong>Sarah Mackenzie</strong> | Stage Manager</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2025/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2025\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
