    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cian-Parker-landscape.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cian-Parker-landscape.jpg?w=1920&amp;ssl=1 1920w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cian-Parker-landscape.jpg?resize=300%2C200&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cian-Parker-landscape.jpg?resize=1024%2C683&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cian-Parker-landscape.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cian-Parker-landscape.jpg?resize=1536%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cian-Parker-landscape.jpg?resize=1120%2C747&amp;ssl=1 1120w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cian-Parker-landscape.jpg?resize=640%2C427&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><em>Photo credit: Kelsey Scott</em></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Cian     Parker&nbsp;Sorry For Your Loss</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Friday, September 26th <br />2pm (Matinee + Masterclass), 8pm (Public Performance)</p><p><a style=\"color: #ded9e9;\" href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/accessibility/#bus-stop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bus Stop Theatre</a></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1454828614549?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBuy Tickets  \n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t<p>Cian Parker (Ngāpuhi) is an award-winning performer, writer, and theatre maker. She graduated from the University of Waikato in 2018 and has toured her original work extensively. Her accolades include the Ngā Manu Pīrere award at the 2019 Te Waka Toi Awards and the 2020 New Zealand Fringe ‘Most Promising Emerging Artist’ award. She received the 2021 Wellington Theatre ‘New Playwright Award’ and a Springboard Award from The Arts Foundation. Recently, Cian worked as the Company Producer for Aotearoa’s first Deaf and hearing theatre company and co-devised their latest bilingual show <em>Where Our Shadows Meet</em>. Roaming Cloud Creative’s second work, <em>All I See</em> toured the UK and Serbia where Cian and her cast mate were the first Māori to perform at the National Theatre in Belgrade, Serbia.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/cian.parker.artist/\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M504 256C504 119 393 8 256 8S8 119 8 256c0 123.78 90.69 226.38 209.25 245V327.69h-63V256h63v-54.64c0-62.15 37-96.48 93.67-96.48 27.14 0 55.52 4.84 55.52 4.84v61h-31.28c-30.8 0-40.41 19.12-40.41 38.73V256h68.78l-11 71.69h-57.78V501C413.31 482.38 504 379.78 504 256z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/cian.parker.artist/\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M224.1 141c-63.6 0-114.9 51.3-114.9 114.9s51.3 114.9 114.9 114.9S339 319.5 339 255.9 287.7 141 224.1 141zm0 189.6c-41.1 0-74.7-33.5-74.7-74.7s33.5-74.7 74.7-74.7 74.7 33.5 74.7 74.7-33.6 74.7-74.7 74.7zm146.4-194.3c0 14.9-12 26.8-26.8 26.8-14.9 0-26.8-12-26.8-26.8s12-26.8 26.8-26.8 26.8 12 26.8 26.8zm76.1 27.2c-1.7-35.9-9.9-67.7-36.2-93.9-26.2-26.2-58-34.4-93.9-36.2-37-2.1-147.9-2.1-184.9 0-35.8 1.7-67.6 9.9-93.9 36.1s-34.4 58-36.2 93.9c-2.1 37-2.1 147.9 0 184.9 1.7 35.9 9.9 67.7 36.2 93.9s58 34.4 93.9 36.2c37 2.1 147.9 2.1 184.9 0 35.9-1.7 67.7-9.9 93.9-36.2 26.2-26.2 34.4-58 36.2-93.9 2.1-37 2.1-147.8 0-184.8zM398.8 388c-7.8 19.6-22.9 34.7-42.6 42.6-29.5 11.7-99.5 9-132.1 9s-102.7 2.6-132.1-9c-19.6-7.8-34.7-22.9-42.6-42.6-11.7-29.5-9-99.5-9-132.1s-2.6-102.7 9-132.1c7.8-19.6 22.9-34.7 42.6-42.6 29.5-11.7 99.5-9 132.1-9s102.7-2.6 132.1 9c19.6 7.8 34.7 22.9 42.6 42.6 11.7 29.5 9 99.5 9 132.1s2.7 102.7-9 132.1z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1200\" height=\"1800\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sorry-for-Your-Loss-photoKelsyScott.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sorry-for-Your-Loss-photoKelsyScott.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sorry-for-Your-Loss-photoKelsyScott.jpg?resize=200%2C300&amp;ssl=1 200w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sorry-for-Your-Loss-photoKelsyScott.jpg?resize=683%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 683w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sorry-for-Your-Loss-photoKelsyScott.jpg?resize=768%2C1152&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sorry-for-Your-Loss-photoKelsyScott.jpg?resize=1024%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sorry-for-Your-Loss-photoKelsyScott.jpg?resize=1120%2C1680&amp;ssl=1 1120w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sorry-for-Your-Loss-photoKelsyScott.jpg?resize=640%2C960&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Sorry For Your Loss</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\tA heartfelt and hilarious story about growing up on the mean streets of Aotearoa (New Zealand) with a sometimes-there-mostly-not Dad. Cian Parker shares her story about reclaiming her heritage when she is unexpectedly introduced to a father and a family she didn’t know existed.Cian has teamed up with director and dramaturg Laura Haughey who brings her unique physical approach to storytelling in this vibrant, award-winning piece of devised theatre. Live music by Andy Duggan accompanies the performance.   <em>Sorry For Your Loss</em> is about the power of wāhine (women); and the gift of strength from one woman to another.<p>Performances of <em>Sorry For Your Loss</em> at Prismatic 2025 will feature artistically integrated ASL interpretation by Gaitrie Persaud-Killings.</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Personnel</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Cian Parker</strong> | Writer / Performer<br /><strong>Gaitrie Persaud-Killings</strong> | ASL Interpreter / Performer<br /><strong>Laura Haughey</strong> | Director / Dramaturg<br /><strong>Andy Duggan</strong> | Musician<br /><strong>Alec Forbes</strong> | Technician</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Pisuwin-346832991_942014243680661_4538303676708427131_n.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Pisuwin-346832991_942014243680661_4538303676708427131_n.jpg?w=1920&amp;ssl=1 1920w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Pisuwin-346832991_942014243680661_4538303676708427131_n.jpg?resize=300%2C200&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Pisuwin-346832991_942014243680661_4538303676708427131_n.jpg?resize=1024%2C683&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Pisuwin-346832991_942014243680661_4538303676708427131_n.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Pisuwin-346832991_942014243680661_4538303676708427131_n.jpg?resize=1536%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Pisuwin-346832991_942014243680661_4538303676708427131_n.jpg?resize=1120%2C747&amp;ssl=1 1120w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/3-website-Pisuwin-346832991_942014243680661_4538303676708427131_n.jpg?resize=640%2C427&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2025/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2025\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
