    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"1914\" height=\"1366\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaitrie-Persaud-Killings-e1753723322589.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaitrie-Persaud-Killings-e1753723322589.jpg?w=1914&amp;ssl=1 1914w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaitrie-Persaud-Killings-e1753723322589.jpg?resize=300%2C214&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaitrie-Persaud-Killings-e1753723322589.jpg?resize=1024%2C731&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaitrie-Persaud-Killings-e1753723322589.jpg?resize=768%2C548&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaitrie-Persaud-Killings-e1753723322589.jpg?resize=1536%2C1096&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaitrie-Persaud-Killings-e1753723322589.jpg?resize=1120%2C799&amp;ssl=1 1120w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaitrie-Persaud-Killings-e1753723322589.jpg?resize=640%2C457&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1914px) 100vw, 1914px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Gaitrie Persaud-Killings</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><em>Performances of </em>Sorry For Your Loss<em> at Bus Stop Theatre will feature artistically integrated ASL interpretation by Gaitrie Persaud-Killings.&nbsp;</em></p>\n<p>Friday, September 26th&nbsp;<br>\n2pm (Matinee + Masterclass) &amp; 8pm (Public Performance) </p>\n<p>Runtime: 60 minutes</p>\n<p><a style=\"color: #ded9e9;\" href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/accessibility/#bus-stop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bus Stop Theatre</a></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1454828614549?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBuy Tickets  \n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/tpersaud2\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M504 256C504 119 393 8 256 8S8 119 8 256c0 123.78 90.69 226.38 209.25 245V327.69h-63V256h63v-54.64c0-62.15 37-96.48 93.67-96.48 27.14 0 55.52 4.84 55.52 4.84v61h-31.28c-30.8 0-40.41 19.12-40.41 38.73V256h68.78l-11 71.69h-57.78V501C413.31 482.38 504 379.78 504 256z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.instagram.com/enchante091216/\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M224.1 141c-63.6 0-114.9 51.3-114.9 114.9s51.3 114.9 114.9 114.9S339 319.5 339 255.9 287.7 141 224.1 141zm0 189.6c-41.1 0-74.7-33.5-74.7-74.7s33.5-74.7 74.7-74.7 74.7 33.5 74.7 74.7-33.6 74.7-74.7 74.7zm146.4-194.3c0 14.9-12 26.8-26.8 26.8-14.9 0-26.8-12-26.8-26.8s12-26.8 26.8-26.8 26.8 12 26.8 26.8zm76.1 27.2c-1.7-35.9-9.9-67.7-36.2-93.9-26.2-26.2-58-34.4-93.9-36.2-37-2.1-147.9-2.1-184.9 0-35.8 1.7-67.6 9.9-93.9 36.1s-34.4 58-36.2 93.9c-2.1 37-2.1 147.9 0 184.9 1.7 35.9 9.9 67.7 36.2 93.9s58 34.4 93.9 36.2c37 2.1 147.9 2.1 184.9 0 35.9-1.7 67.7-9.9 93.9-36.2 26.2-26.2 34.4-58 36.2-93.9 2.1-37 2.1-147.8 0-184.8zM398.8 388c-7.8 19.6-22.9 34.7-42.6 42.6-29.5 11.7-99.5 9-132.1 9s-102.7 2.6-132.1-9c-19.6-7.8-34.7-22.9-42.6-42.6-11.7-29.5-9-99.5-9-132.1s-2.6-102.7 9-132.1c7.8-19.6 22.9-34.7 42.6-42.6 29.5-11.7 99.5-9 132.1-9s102.7-2.6 132.1 9c19.6 7.8 34.7 22.9 42.6 42.6 11.7 29.5 9 99.5 9 132.1s2.7 102.7-9 132.1z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\tGaitrie is a Tkaronto-based actor and theatremaker whose work bridges the Deaf and hearing communities through the power of physical theatre. Specializing in the development of expressive facial and body language, she creates inclusive performance environments where Deaf and hearing actors collaborate seamlessly on stage. With a deep commitment to her craft, Gaitrie continually challenges herself by exploring new techniques and learning from mentors who specialize in physical theatre styles.She is the founder of Phoenix the Fire, a dynamic theatre and film hub dedicated to supporting Deaf artists in discovering their talents. The hub also provides ASL theatre, music and film interpretation services, contributing to greater accessibility and representation in the arts.<p>Her screen work includes roles such as Camila, the Deaf Librarian on <em>Nickelodeon Jr.'s Blue’s Clues &amp; You</em> and Simmi on the <em>CBC Kids</em> series <em>Silly Paws</em> – the latter of which earned her the CBC Youth Short Content Award. She also stars as Arianna, a spirited reporter on the acclaimed series <em>Squeaky the Wheel</em>, which has received four award nominations to date. Additionally, Gaitrie serves as a news anchor for Sign1News, powered by CNN, bringing accessible news to the Deaf community.</p>A passionate Deaf music performer, Gaitrie brings her love for music to the stage through expressive, rhythmic performance that connects audiences beyond sound. She recently performed as an ASL music interpreter at the 2025 JUNO Awards, a proud moment that reflects her dedication to celebrating music through visual language.\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2025/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2025\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
      }
    ],
