self by exploring new techniques and learning from mentors who specialize in physical theatre styles.She is the founder of Phoenix the Fire, a dynamic theatre and film hub dedicated to supporting Deaf artists in discovering their talents. The hub also provides ASL theatre, music and film interpretation services, contributing to greater accessibility and representation in the arts.<p>Her screen work includes roles such as Camila, the Deaf Librarian on <em>Nickelodeon Jr.'s Blue’s Clues &amp; You</em> and Simmi on the <em>CBC Kids</em> series <em>Silly Paws</em> – the latter of which earned her the CBC Youth Short Content Award. She also stars as Arianna, a spirited reporter on the acclaimed series <em>Squeaky the Wheel</em>, which has received four award nominations to date. Additionally, Gaitrie serves as a news anchor for Sign1News, powered by CNN, bringing accessible news to the Deaf community.</p>A passionate Deaf music performer, Gaitrie brings her love for music to the stage through expressive, rhythmic performance that connects audiences beyond sound. She recently performed as an ASL music interpreter at the 2025 JUNO Awards, a proud moment that reflects her dedication to celebrating music through visual language.\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2025/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2025\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
