\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/rhodniedesir\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M224.1 141c-63.6 0-114.9 51.3-114.9 114.9s51.3 114.9 114.9 114.9S339 319.5 339 255.9 287.7 141 224.1 141zm0 189.6c-41.1 0-74.7-33.5-74.7-74.7s33.5-74.7 74.7-74.7 74.7 33.5 74.7 74.7-33.6 74.7-74.7 74.7zm146.4-194.3c0 14.9-12 26.8-26.8 26.8-14.9 0-26.8-12-26.8-26.8s12-26.8 26.8-26.8 26.8 12 26.8 26.8zm76.1 27.2c-1.7-35.9-9.9-67.7-36.2-93.9-26.2-26.2-58-34.4-93.9-36.2-37-2.1-147.9-2.1-184.9 0-35.8 1.7-67.6 9.9-93.9 36.1s-34.4 58-36.2 93.9c-2.1 37-2.1 147.9 0 184.9 1.7 35.9 9.9 67.7 36.2 93.9s58 34.4 93.9 36.2c37 2.1 147.9 2.1 184.9 0 35.9-1.7 67.7-9.9 93.9-36.2 26.2-26.2 34.4-58 36.2-93.9 2.1-37 2.1-147.8 0-184.8zM398.8 388c-7.8 19.6-22.9 34.7-42.6 42.6-29.5 11.7-99.5 9-132.1 9s-102.7 2.6-132.1-9c-19.6-7.8-34.7-22.9-42.6-42.6-11.7-29.5-9-99.5-9-132.1s-2.6-102.7 9-132.1c7.8-19.6 22.9-34.7 42.6-42.6 29.5-11.7 99.5-9 132.1-9s102.7-2.6 132.1 9c19.6 7.8 34.7 22.9 42.6 42.6 11.7 29.5 9 99.5 9 132.1s2.7 102.7-9 132.1z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t<p>Choreographer-documentary artist and artistic director of RD Créations, Rhodnie Désir, has created over 30 productions, including the masterful Symphonie de coeurs avec orchestre, the acclaimed <em>BOW'T TRAIL Rétrospek</em> and her pioneering <em>BOW'T TRAIL</em>, which earned her two Prix de la danse de Montréal (2020), the Envol Prize and the coveted Grand Prix de la danse, as well as a nomination for the Dora Mavor Moore Awards (2025 Outstanding Touring Production).</p><p><em>\"Each of my works is created and designed as a way to transmit, awaken, unveil and encounter live, past and present memories of the world. This occurs through cultural mediation, particularly with young people, and by recreating works based on the convergence of ancestral rhythms (drums and voice).\" | RD</em></p>Rhodnie Désir's documentary and Afro-contemporary choreographic signature is rooted in African and Afro-descendant rhythmic languages from places like her homeland (Haiti), as well as the rest of the Caribbean, and Central and Sub-Saharan Africa. A performer of remarkable power and uncompromising integrity, she surprises by her great connectivity to humanity. Her unique approach, her words, her performances and her civic actions have brought her strong international recognition and have made her a guest speaker at numerous organizations and universities, as well as at the UNESCO, among others.Rhodnie Désir holds degrees in communications and marketing from Université de Montréal and HEC Montréal, in Afro-contemporary dance (Programme de formation professionnelle en danses africaines / Compagnie Nyata Nyata) and two specializations in entrepreneurship.An entrepreneur at heart, she has led the Dêzam organization, which she created in 2008, for 10 years. Through it, she set up more than 2,500 youth cultural actions. In 2017, she founded her dance company, RD Creations. In January 2021, she was chosen as one of the \"25 to watch\" by Dance Magazine in New York. In April 2021, she was nominated by APAP for the prestigious career award The award of merit for achievement in the performing arts 2021, alongside Yo-Yo Ma and Ronald K. Brown. In 2022, she received the “Danseuse de l’année” award at the Gala Dynastie she became the first Associate Artist of the famous Place des Arts institution in Montreal. In the fall of 2022, she was honored by the Dance Collection Danse (DCD) Hall of Fame with the Sandra Faire Next Generation Award. In 2025, she joined the SAGES cohort at the University of Montreal.<p><em>\"Maybe creation is about accepting that, with every millisecond, we can endlessly re-create ourselves, to better come to terms with the world in which we exist.\" | RD</em></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/BOWTTRAILRhodnieDesir.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/BOWTTRAILRhodnieDesir.jpg?w=1920&amp;ssl=1 1920w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/BOWTTRAILRhodnieDesir.jpg?resize=300%2C200&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/BOWTTRAILRhodnieDesir.jpg?resize=1024%2C683&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/BOWTTRAILRhodnieDesir.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/BOWTTRAILRhodnieDesir.jpg?resize=1536%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/BOWTTRAILRhodnieDesir.jpg?resize=1120%2C747&amp;ssl=1 1120w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/BOWTTRAILRhodnieDesir.jpg?resize=640%2C427&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>BOW’T TRAIL Rétrospek</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<em>BOW’T TRAIL Rétrospek</em> is an interdisciplinary dance piece by RD Créations, choreographed by Rhodnie Désir.Since 2015, Rhodnie has been exploring the Americas in search of Afro-descendant cultures, including Martinique, Haiti, Brazil, Mexico, Halifax, and New Orleans. The choreographer, driven by a desire and a need to transcend her origins, has been immersing herself in the African cultures and rhythms of the peoples who were taken to these lands. The resulting performance piece, <em>BOW’T TRAIL Rétrospek</em>, is a conversation between the present and the past, channeled through the body of Rhodnie Désir, in which more than 130 testimonies collected on lands of the Americas still reside.\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Personnel:</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Rhodnie Désir</strong> | Choreographer/Dancer/Artistic Director/Vocal Compositions<br /><strong>Isabelle Poirier</strong> | Creative Support<br /><strong>Engone Endong</strong> | Musician, Beatmaker, Music Composer<br /><strong>Jahsun</strong> | Musician<br /><strong>Tristan-Olivier Breiding</strong> | Lighting<br /><strong>Pierre-Alexandre Poirier-Guay </strong> | Sound</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/prismatic-2025/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBack to 2025\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>"
