    "http://schema.org/headline": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "2025 Pisuwin"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<img width=\"902\" height=\"1280\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pisuwin-e1749749100489.jpg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pisuwin-e1749749100489.jpg?w=902&amp;ssl=1 902w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pisuwin-e1749749100489.jpg?resize=211%2C300&amp;ssl=1 211w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pisuwin-e1749749100489.jpg?resize=722%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 722w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pisuwin-e1749749100489.jpg?resize=768%2C1090&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pisuwin-e1749749100489.jpg?resize=640%2C908&amp;ssl=1 640w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 902px) 100vw, 902px\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img width=\"150\" height=\"115\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Atlantic-Ballet-cropped-logo-newone-150x115.png\" alt=\"\" />\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Pisuwin</h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p>Sunday, September 28th | 7:30 PM</p><p>Runtime: 105 minutes (1h45m) </p><p><a style=\"color: #ded9e9;\" href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/index.php/accessibility#spatz-theatre\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spatz Theatre</a></p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1407548819409?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBuy Tickets  \n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t<p>From award-winning director and choreographer Igor Dobrovolskiy, and multidisciplinary artist Nipahtuwet Naka Wespahtuwet (Possesom) Paul (Wolastoqiyik, Sitansisk First Nation), <em>Pisuwin</em> is a first ever Wolastoq contemporary story-ballet set to the soaring music of Polaris Prize and Juno award-winning composer Jeremy Dutcher (Wolastoqiyik, Neqotkuk First Nation).</p><p>Based on a Wolastoq tale, this multidisciplinary piece reflects on the current state of dis-ease in our world, illuminating a path to wholeness and rebalance. The project features eight dancers and blends Indigenous storytelling and ballet, redefining this classical form for a diverse, savvy, and contemporary audience. Electronic sound, industrial landscapes, and digital projection, juxtaposed with Wolastoq visual motifs of the spiritual and natural world, create the Indigenous cosmology within which the story takes place.</p><em>Pisuwin</em> pushes us to confront our greed and alienation, while inspiring us to take a different path; one of connection, community and wholeness.\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.atlanticballet.ca/en/event/pisuwin/\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tGlobe\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 496 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M336.5 160C322 70.7 287.8 8 248 8s-74 62.7-88.5 152h177zM152 256c0 22.2 1.2 43.5 3.3 64h185.3c2.1-20.5 3.3-41.8 3.3-64s-1.2-43.5-3.3-64H155.3c-2.1 20.5-3.3 41.8-3.3 64zm324.7-96c-28.6-67.9-86.5-120.4-158-141.6 24.4 33.8 41.2 84.7 50 141.6h108zM177.2 18.4C105.8 39.6 47.8 92.1 19.3 160h108c8.7-56.9 25.5-107.8 49.9-141.6zM487.4 192H372.7c2.1 21 3.3 42.5 3.3 64s-1.2 43-3.3 64h114.6c5.5-20.5 8.6-41.8 8.6-64s-3.1-43.5-8.5-64zM120 256c0-21.5 1.2-43 3.3-64H8.6C3.2 212.5 0 233.8 0 256s3.2 43.5 8.6 64h114.6c-2-21-3.2-42.5-3.2-64zm39.5 96c14.5 89.3 48.7 152 88.5 152s74-62.7 88.5-152h-177zm159.3 141.6c71.4-21.2 129.4-73.7 158-141.6h-108c-8.8 56.9-25.6 107.8-50 141.6zM19.3 352c28.6 67.9 86.5 120.4 158 141.6-24.4-33.8-41.2-84.7-50-141.6h-108z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/AtlanticBalletAtlantique\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFacebook\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M504 256C504 119 393 8 256 8S8 119 8 256c0 123.78 90.69 226.38 209.25 245V327.69h-63V256h63v-54.64c0-62.15 37-96.48 93.67-96.48 27.14 0 55.52 4.84 55.52 4.84v61h-31.28c-30.8 0-40.41 19.12-40.41 38.73V256h68.78l-11 71.69h-57.78V501C413.31 482.38 504 379.78 504 256z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/atlanticballetatlantique/\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInstagram\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M224.1 141c-63.6 0-114.9 51.3-114.9 114.9s51.3 114.9 114.9 114.9S339 319.5 339 255.9 287.7 141 224.1 141zm0 189.6c-41.1 0-74.7-33.5-74.7-74.7s33.5-74.7 74.7-74.7 74.7 33.5 74.7 74.7-33.6 74.7-74.7 74.7zm146.4-194.3c0 14.9-12 26.8-26.8 26.8-14.9 0-26.8-12-26.8-26.8s12-26.8 26.8-26.8 26.8 12 26.8 26.8zm76.1 27.2c-1.7-35.9-9.9-67.7-36.2-93.9-26.2-26.2-58-34.4-93.9-36.2-37-2.1-147.9-2.1-184.9 0-35.8 1.7-67.6 9.9-93.9 36.1s-34.4 58-36.2 93.9c-2.1 37-2.1 147.9 0 184.9 1.7 35.9 9.9 67.7 36.2 93.9s58 34.4 93.9 36.2c37 2.1 147.9 2.1 184.9 0 35.9-1.7 67.7-9.9 93.9-36.2 26.2-26.2 34.4-58 36.2-93.9 2.1-37 2.1-147.8 0-184.8zM398.8 388c-7.8 19.6-22.9 34.7-42.6 42.6-29.5 11.7-99.5 9-132.1 9s-102.7 2.6-132.1-9c-19.6-7.8-34.7-22.9-42.6-42.6-11.7-29.5-9-99.5-9-132.1s-2.6-102.7 9-132.1c7.8-19.6 22.9-34.7 42.6-42.6 29.5-11.7 99.5-9 132.1-9s102.7-2.6 132.1 9c19.6 7.8 34.7 22.9 42.6 42.6 11.7 29.5 9 99.5 9 132.1s2.7 102.7-9 132.1z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCY2mr2BsGR0GpsGew3QQbIA/featured\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tYoutube\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 576 512\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M549.655 124.083c-6.281-23.65-24.787-42.276-48.284-48.597C458.781 64 288 64 288 64S117.22 64 74.629 75.486c-23.497 6.322-42.003 24.947-48.284 48.597-11.412 42.867-11.412 132.305-11.412 132.305s0 89.438 11.412 132.305c6.281 23.65 24.787 41.5 48.284 47.821C117.22 448 288 448 288 448s170.78 0 213.371-11.486c23.497-6.321 42.003-24.171 48.284-47.821 11.412-42.867 11.412-132.305 11.412-132.305s0-89.438-11.412-132.305zm-317.51 213.508V175.185l142.739 81.205-142.739 81.201z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Full Program ↓&nbsp;</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<iframe width=\"350\" height=\"400\" src=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/plugins/pdfjs-viewer-for-elementor//assets/js/pdfjs/web/viewer.html?file=https://prismaticfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/PISUWIN-PROGRAM.pdf\"></iframe>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2>Personnel</h2>\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<p><strong>Igor Dobrovolskiy</strong> | Artistic Director/ Choreographer<br /><strong>Nipahtuwet Naka Wespahtuwet (Possesom) Pau</strong>l | Co-Director<br /><strong>Jeremy Dutcher</strong> | Composer<br /><strong>Jera Wolfe</strong> | Principal Dancer<br /><strong>Andy Moro</strong> | Costume, Set, and Projection Design<br /><strong>Pierre Lavoie</strong> | Lighting Design<br /><strong>Keira Loughran</strong> | Dramaturg<br /><strong>Emma Hassencahl-Perley</strong> | Costume Design<br /><strong>Oakley Rain Wysote Gray</strong> | Beading and Costume Production<br /><strong>Dawson Sacobie (M3D14)</strong> | Soundscape Design<br /><strong>Olga Petieau</strong> | Dancer<br /><strong>Laura Flydorf</strong> | Dancer</p>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 1000\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M646 125C629 125 613 133 604 142L308 442C296 454 292 471 292 487 292 504 296 521 308 533L604 854C617 867 629 875 646 875 663 875 679 871 692 858 704 846 713 829 713 812 713 796 708 779 692 767L438 487 692 225C700 217 708 204 708 187 708 171 704 154 692 142 675 129 663 125 646 125Z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 1000\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M696 533C708 521 713 504 713 487 713 471 708 454 696 446L400 146C388 133 375 125 354 125 338 125 325 129 313 142 300 154 292 171 292 187 292 204 296 221 308 233L563 492 304 771C292 783 288 800 288 817 288 833 296 850 308 863 321 871 338 875 354 875 371 875 388 867 400 854L696 533Z\"></path></svg>\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t<em>Photo credits: Photo Geegee</em>\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://prismaticfestival.com/ind